IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pngf-rules`

§ `Tests`

base MEANS `Service record` OF TRUE, Date 1 3 1942, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT `a member of the Forces under s 3` base
#ASSERT `the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` base
#ASSERT NOT (`a member of the Forces under s 3` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 3 9 1945, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `a member of the Forces under s 3` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 3 9 1939, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a member of the Forces under s 3` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 1 3 1942, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 1 3 1942, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 1 3 1942, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 1 3 1942, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commonwealth is liable under s 5` (`Service record` OF TRUE, Date 1 3 1942, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT (`the forces position for` base)'s `pension is inalienable`
